CLAHE Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization


Face Match Pipeline Using Dlib:

This pipeline verifies the student's identity in real time during an online exam using Dlib's HOG-based frontal face detector for face detection and 
Dlib's ResNet-based face recognition for identity matching. 
This approach offers good accuracy, is efficient on CPU, and performs well even under variable lighting and pose conditions. 
All identity checks, including timestamps, match results and face crops (if mismatched), are logged in a secure database for audit.

i. Webcam Frame Capture

Frames are continuously captured from the student's webcam for identity verification throughout the exam.

ii. Face Detection Using Dlib HOG Detector

Every frame is passed through Dlib's HOG-based frontal face detector, which detects faces and provides bounding box coordinates.
Before detection, CLAHE is applied in the LAB color space to normalize lighting conditions.

If no face is detected, the absence is logged with timestamp, and monitoring is continued.

If a face is detected, the cropped face ROI is extracted using the bounding box and passed to the embedding generator.

iii. Face Embedding Generation (Dlib ResNet)

The cropped and aligned face is passed to Dlib's ResNet-based face recognition model to generate a 128D face embedding that encodes the person's identity.
The same is done with the pre-registered reference image (from enrollment). Both embeddings are then compared.

iv. Face Matching and Verification
Compute Euclidean distance between the live face embedding and the registered embedding. 
If distance ≤ threshold (typically 0.6) the identity is verified successfully and the monitoring continues. If distance > threshold, 
the system logs the mismatch event with timestamp, saves the cropped face for review and raises a warning to the proctor.

v. Continuous or Periodic Identity Check

Face match is done periodically every CHECK_INTERVAL seconds for enhanced security.

vi. Logging and Audit Trail

All checks including timestamp, match status (pass/fail) and cropped face image (for mismatches) are recorded. This enables reliable post-exam review and strengthens academic integrity.
